  <selectionEntries>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Asuryani" hidden="false" id="d799-5beb-3b5c-80a0" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <constraints>
        <constraint type="min" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" shared="true" id="abd1-87f4-f7e2-c0e0" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
        <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" shared="true" id="3d4d-c591-fb68-8b27" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
      </constraints>
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Aspects of War" typeId="90b9-7fab-87db-aed3" typeName="Reactions" hidden="false" id="fddb-17f5-20f4-4327">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="c627-4637-8de5-65fb">(once per battle, any phase). This Advanced Reaction is available only to units in an Asuryani Detachment. It uses a point of the Reaction Allotment as normal and obeys all other Reaction restrictions unless noted. It may be made once per battle, in any phase, when an enemy unit does one of the following: Ends a move within 12" and line of sight of a unit in an Asuryani Detachment. Makes a Shooting Attack targeting a unit in an Asuryani Detachment. Declares a Charge targeting a unit in an Asuryani Detachment. The Reactive Player may immediately choose one of the following: Move: The Reacting unit moves up to its unmodified Initiative in inches in any direction. In a unit with mixed Initiative, use the highest unmodified value. Vehicles may pivot once up to 180° and then move up to 8" directly forwards. Shoot: The Reacting unit makes a Shooting Attack, resolved immediately, against the unit that triggered the Reaction. No indirect attacks (including Barrage or other weapons or rules that ignore line of sight); Vehicles may only fire Defensive weapons. Template weapons may only be used if the target is within 8", and must use Wall of Death. The unit counts as Stationary and may fire weapons of any type as though it had not moved. Disorder: The Reacting unit counts any charges made against it this turn as Disordered.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <categoryLinks>
        <categoryLink targetId="e90d-e5a8-f42d-da84" id="24d5-297b-f3a2-1243" primary="true" name="Allegiance:" />
        <categoryLink targetId="3c8e-5a1d-9b47-e2f0" id="6cd9-5453-4603-473f" primary="false" name="Xenos Army" />
      </categoryLinks>
