          <selectionEntries>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="The Crucible of Blood" hidden="false" id="6e83-b6f3-c361-f4b2" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
              <rules>
                <rule name="Effects" id="9dee-8cf1-03c9-e4b9" hidden="false">
                  <description>Units eligible to take a Wave Serpent as a Dedicated Transport may instead take a single Falcon as a Dedicated Transport if the unit numbers 5 models or less. Falcon Squadrons may be selected as non-Compulsory Troops choices. Firestorm Squadrons and Night Spinner Squadrons may be selected as Elites choices. Models with the Bonesinger Companions Special Rule may ignore its joining restrictions, and may instead join any unit with the Infantry Unit Type and the Asuryani Sub-type. The Detachment may ignore the 0-1 limit on Bonesinger Conclaves, and may take them as non-Compulsory Troops choices. If the army's Warlord does not have the Unique Sub-type, it gains the Path of the Shaper Special Rule.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Limitations" id="b8a7-e216-4b1b-f43e" hidden="false">
                  <description>All Infantry units in the Detachment must begin the battle Embarked on a model with the Transport Sub-type. Any Infantry models (on the battlefield or in Reserves) not Embarked on a Transport at the beginning of the first Game Turn are removed as casualties. At least one Bonesinger Conclave must be selected. An Allied Detachment may not use this World-Rune. The Detachment may not select any units with the Wraith Sub-type.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <categoryLinks>
                <categoryLink targetId="d494-e450-d4aa-579a" id="9c1b-b846-7745-1a82" primary="true" name="Rite of War:" />
              </categoryLinks>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Echoes of the Fallen" hidden="false" id="1485-1121-da0e-dbe7" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
              <rules>
                <rule name="Effects" id="4057-7caa-35c9-c4a6" hidden="false">
                  <description>A single Wraith Guide, Wraithseer, or single-model Wraithlord Conclave may be taken as a Compulsory HQ choice. It gains the Path of Command Special Rule and the Character Sub-type (if it lacks it), and must be the Warlord. If not already equipped with Guide Stones, it may take them for +15 points. A Wraithseer taken this way does not count towards its usual 0-1 limit. Wraithblades and Wraithguard may be taken as Troops. Wraithblades and Wraithguard taken as Compulsory Troops gain the Line Sub-type. Wraithblades and Wraithguard do not count towards the number of Wraith units allowed by the Wraith Guide Special Rule.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Limitations" id="d845-ab3d-f385-8df9" hidden="false">
                  <description>The Detachment must include a Wraith Guide. The Detachment must include at least as many Wraith units as non-Wraith units. Guardian Officer Cadres, Guardian Defenders, and Storm Guardians are not counted. An Allied Detachment may not use this World-Rune. The Detachment may only select a single Fast Attack choice. An army containing this Detachment may never roll to Seize the Initiative. The Detachment counts as Distrusted Allies to all other Aeldari Sub-factions.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <categoryLinks>
                <categoryLink targetId="d494-e450-d4aa-579a" id="0b2d-5016-428d-900d" primary="true" name="Rite of War:" />
              </categoryLinks>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="The Hunter's Moon" hidden="false" id="7b54-6c8d-6ece-8cd8" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
              <rules>
                <rule name="Effects" id="8525-996a-f66a-90cd" hidden="false">
                  <description>Any Independent Character may take an Outcast Cloak for +10 points. If it does, it may also gain the Skirmish Sub-type and the Scout Special Rule at no extra cost. Any model with the Character Sub-type may take a Ranger long rifle for +10 points. One model in each Infantry unit, that does not have the Character Sub-type, may take a Gloom-Field for +15 points. All Infantry models gain the Move Through Cover Special Rule. Shroud Runners gain the Line Sub-type. Rangers gain the Pathfinder Special Rule and lose the Support Squad Special Rule.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Limitations" id="04c1-12ad-5bb7-0b79" hidden="false">
                  <description>All Vehicle models must begin play in Reserves. The Detachment cannot include more Heavy Support choices than Fast Attack choices. All Compulsory Troops choices must be Rangers.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <categoryLinks>
                <categoryLink targetId="d494-e450-d4aa-579a" id="a825-a942-661b-b7ca" primary="true" name="Rite of War:" />
              </categoryLinks>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="The Serpent Host" hidden="false" id="7904-b140-5846-d462" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
              <rules>
                <rule name="Effects" id="3df0-d132-e040-20fb" hidden="false">
                  <description>Windrider Squads do not have the Support Squad Special Rule. Windrider Squads taken as Compulsory Troops gain the Line Sub-type. Vyper Squadrons may be taken as non-Compulsory Troops. Shining Spears may be taken as Elites choices. A single unit made up entirely of models with Aspect Shrine (Shining Spear) may be selected without restriction, whichever Aspect Shrine upgrades the army has. It still uses a Force Organisation slot as normal.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Limitations" id="f481-19bb-28ad-c645" hidden="false">
                  <description>The Detachment must select more units equipped with Skyrunner Jetbikes, Vyper Jetbikes, or Raptor Jetbikes than units without. Compulsory HQ choices must be made up entirely of models with Skyrunner Jetbikes. Any unit made up entirely of non-Cavalry models that does not begin play Embarked on a Transport, and any Vehicle without the Transport or Fast Sub-type, must begin play in Reserve if the mission allows. If it does not, the unit deploys as normal. The Detachment may not select any Fortification choices.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <categoryLinks>
                <categoryLink targetId="d494-e450-d4aa-579a" id="738d-d2dd-8a6e-0dce" primary="true" name="Rite of War:" />
              </categoryLinks>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="The Shattered Chains" hidden="false" id="a672-9b42-85fe-cd8e" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
              <rules>
                <rule name="Effects" id="7097-fb4b-7423-5322" hidden="false">
                  <description>Independent Characters not selected as a Primarch choice may select a Guardian Officer Cadre as part of the same Force Organisation slot. It is a Retinue Squad: minimum 2 models, uses no slot, counts as part of the Independent Character's unit, and must deploy with it; the Independent Character may not voluntarily leave it. Its models lose the Guardian Officers Special Rule and the Character Sub-type, and gain the Chosen Warriors Special Rule. If the Independent Character has a Skyrunner Jetbike, the Retinue Squad must all have Skyrunner Jetbikes; if not, none of them may. The Detachment may ignore the 0-1 limit on Guardian Officer Cadres, and may take them as HQ choices. Cadres taken as HQ lose the Guardian Officers Special Rule and the Character Sub-type, and gain the Chosen Warriors Special Rule. Guardian Defenders may be selected as Elites choices. When taken this way, all Guardian Defender and Defender Platform models in the unit have BS 5. Storm Guardians may be selected as Elites choices. When taken this way, all Storm Guardian and Defender Platform models in the unit have WS 5. All models without Aspect Shrine (X) or the Wraith Sub-type gain Stubborn. Models without a Leadership Characteristic instead ignore Crew Shaken results on the Vehicle Damage table.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Limitations" id="eea5-c548-2f66-7cd1" hidden="false">
                  <description>The Detachment counts as Distrusted Allies to all other Aeldari Sub-factions. All Compulsory Troops choices must be Guardian Defenders or Storm Guardians. All Compulsory Troops choices must take the maximum number of models possible (not including Defender Platforms).</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <categoryLinks>
                <categoryLink targetId="d494-e450-d4aa-579a" id="a3c2-e05a-ae81-b522" primary="true" name="Rite of War:" />
              </categoryLinks>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="The Sword-Wind" hidden="false" id="275c-cebf-109f-1aac" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
              <rules>
                <rule name="Effects" id="a758-2258-b546-9e9c" hidden="false">
                  <description>The Detachment may include up to two Aspect Exarch units instead of one. An Autarch may select a second, different Aspect Shrine upgrade, paying its points cost and gaining all its Unit Types, Sub-types, Special Rules, and Wargear.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Limitations" id="e0ae-524a-b2a3-660d" hidden="false">
                  <description>The Detachment must include an Autarch, who must be the Warlord, unless a Phoenix Lord is present, in which case the Phoenix Lord must be the Warlord. An Allied Detachment may not use this World-Rune. The Detachment may not include more non-Infantry units than Infantry units. Aspect Exarchs, Bonesinger Conclaves, Guardian Officer Cadres, Guardian Defenders, and Storm Guardians are not counted.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <categoryLinks>
                <categoryLink targetId="d494-e450-d4aa-579a" id="ff41-4f06-3d05-3a14" primary="true" name="Rite of War:" />
              </categoryLinks>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="The Tears of Lileath" hidden="false" id="011a-efe9-93fe-2d05" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
              <rules>
                <rule name="Effects" id="d662-ddd4-5ff4-0e28" hidden="false">
                  <description>A single Farseer gains the Path of Command Special Rule. The Detachment may ignore the 0-1 limit on Seer Council units. All non-Vehicle models gain Adamantium Will (6+). Models with the Psyker Sub-type gain Adamantium Will (3+) instead. Guardian Defenders, Storm Guardians, and Vaul's Wrath Support Batteries may add a single Warlock for +35 points (see Seer Council). A Warlock added this way may not be upgraded to a Warlock Skyrunner. Windrider Squads may add a single Warlock Skyrunner for +50 points (see Seer Council). If the Primary Detachment uses this World-Rune, the player may re-roll the roll for first turn or to Seize the Initiative.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Limitations" id="4560-c33e-83b7-2537" hidden="false">
                  <description>The Warlord must be a Farseer or Eldrad Ulthran. An Allied Detachment may not use this World-Rune. The Detachment must include at least one Seer Council selected as an Elites choice. The Detachment cannot include more Psyker units than non-Psyker units. Any unit that suffers Perils of the Warp from a Psychic check is immediately Pinned. This overrides Unit Types that would normally ignore Pinning (such as Cavalry, or a type granting Fearless), but cannot affect units without a Leadership Characteristic.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <categoryLinks>
                <categoryLink targetId="d494-e450-d4aa-579a" id="09ce-e929-ebb0-faee" primary="true" name="Rite of War:" />
              </categoryLinks>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
          </selectionEntries>
        </selectionEntryGroup>
      </selectionEntryGroups>
      <costs>
        <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
      </costs>
    </selectionEntry>
  </selectionEntries>
