  <sharedSelectionEntryGroups>
    <selectionEntryGroup name="Warlord Traits" hidden="false" id="01e7-08db-8a96-85fb">
      <constraints>
        <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="2b09-d849-ac00-08cf" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
      </constraints>
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Ambush of Blades" hidden="false" id="0cfa-a47b-24f4-34b0" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="eab6-fd90-a70d-e7b2" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Ambush of Blades" typeId="a0e6-a7b4-d55d-85b8" typeName="Warlord Trait" hidden="false" id="26a2-e52f-08f4-75a0">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="c68e-2cda-b67b-baca">*This warrior's uncanny senses pierce the fog of war, letting them strike at the precise moment alongside their kin.* - Once per battle, at the start of any phase, the Warlord and any unit they have joined gain Preferred Enemy (Everything!) for that phase only. - The army may make an additional Reaction during the opposing player's Assault phase while the Warlord has not been removed as a casualty.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <categoryLinks>
            <categoryLink targetId="1158-146a-d9a0-39ad" id="0373-2229-f989-ba27" primary="true" name="Warlord Traits:" />
          </categoryLinks>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Falcon's Swiftness" hidden="false" id="e482-01a0-6031-26b1" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="8bf8-89ed-a90d-484b" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Falcon's Swiftness" typeId="a0e6-a7b4-d55d-85b8" typeName="Warlord Trait" hidden="false" id="8af8-400a-c1a8-3f7a">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="c68e-2cda-b67b-baca">*This warrior, and those in their wake, cross broken ruins and blasted battlefields with astonishing certainty.* - The Warlord and any unit they have joined increase their Fleet (X) value by +1, or gain Fleet (1) if they do not have it. The Warlord also gains Pathfinder. - The army may make an additional Reaction during the opposing player's Movement phase while the Warlord has not been removed as a casualty.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <categoryLinks>
            <categoryLink targetId="1158-146a-d9a0-39ad" id="df42-43c1-413b-afff" primary="true" name="Warlord Traits:" />
          </categoryLinks>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Seer of the Shifting Vector" hidden="false" id="5809-c0b9-300c-7298" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="c356-31a2-dcff-8d1a" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Seer of the Shifting Vector" typeId="a0e6-a7b4-d55d-85b8" typeName="Warlord Trait" hidden="false" id="de2f-f254-5a2d-7005">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="c68e-2cda-b67b-baca">*Reading the skeins of destiny, this warrior sees the many possible futures of the coming battle and coordinates their forces accordingly.* - While the Warlord is in Reserves or deployed on the battlefield, the Controlling Player may re-roll failed Reserves rolls. - The army may make an additional Reaction during the opposing player's Shooting phase while the Warlord has not been removed as a casualty.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <categoryLinks>
            <categoryLink targetId="1158-146a-d9a0-39ad" id="9682-e4f9-3d05-9312" primary="true" name="Warlord Traits:" />
          </categoryLinks>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntryGroup>
  </sharedSelectionEntryGroups>
  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Aeldari (X)" id="75bf-7277-e561-2612" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>The civilization keywords represent the major surviving branches of the Aeldari species. Every Aeldari unit has at least one Civilization keyword, shown as X, which determines which armies, detachments and force organizations may include that unit. These keywords work like Legion, Klan or Household affiliations in other factions. Aeldari units may only be selected in armies whose Civilization keyword matches at least one of the unit's listed Civilization keywords unless specifically stated otherwise. Units with several Civilization keywords may be selected in any army matching one or more of them: a Corsair Voidreaver unit with the keywords Anhrathe and Asuryani may be selected in either an Anhrathe army or an Asuryani army; a Harlequin Shadowseer with the Rillietann keyword may be included only in armies permitted to include Rillietann units; an Incubi unit with only the Drukhari keyword may only be selected in a Drukhari army. Unless specifically stated otherwise, Asuryani and Drukhari units may not be selected within the same Primary Detachment; Rillietann units may be included as Allied or Auxiliary units in any Aeldari army; and Anhrathe units may be selected as Primary, Allied or Auxiliary forces alongside either Asuryani or Drukhari armies.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Daemon Primarch" id="6b5f-7a4d-4774-7f0c" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>- Has Independent Character, Eternal Warrior, Fear (2), It Will Not Die (5+), Bulky (6), and Relentless, and always counts as a Character model. - Not affected by Special Rules that negatively modify its Characteristics (other than Wounds), and always resolves Snap Shots at its normal BS. - Immune to Fear (X) and cannot be Pinned. A unit including one automatically passes Pinning and Regroup tests and cannot choose to fail a Morale check due to Our Weapons Are Useless. - When a unit including one fails a Morale check, it does not Fall Back. Instead it suffers D3 automatic Wounds with no Saves of any kind, allocated to a model with the Daemon Primarch or Daemon Unit Type or the Corrupted Sub-type. - Has Precision Strikes (2+) and Precision Shots (2+), and may use them even when it would normally be prevented, including on Snap Shots. - If the army includes any Daemon Primarch models, one of them must be the Warlord. - Counts as having the Daemon and Primarch Unit Types for any rule that affects those types. - A unit made up entirely of Primarch models may ignore Heroic Stand and its penalties for declining a Challenge, unless the Challenge was issued by a Knight, Gargantuan, Titan, Primarch, or Daemon Primarch.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Phoenix Lord" id="1892-3327-95cd-9470" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>- Has Independent Character, Eternal Warrior, Fearless, Relentless, Favoured of Khaine, and Path of Command, and always counts as a Character model. - Not affected by Special Rules that negatively modify its Characteristics (other than Wounds), and always resolves Snap Shots at its normal BS. - Has Precision Strikes (2+) and Precision Shots (2+), and may use them even when it would normally be prevented, including on Snap Shots. - If the army includes any Phoenix Lord models, one of them must be the Warlord. - A unit made up entirely of Phoenix Lord models may ignore Heroic Stand and its penalties for declining a Challenge, unless the Challenge was issued by a Knight, Gargantuan, Titan, Primarch, or Daemon Primarch. - Attacks and effects against a unit with a Phoenix Lord are resolved as if the Phoenix Lord had the Primarch Unit Type. This covers Wargear, Weapons, Special Rules, Psychic Powers, and any other abilities. - May join units and embark on Transports as though it had the Infantry Unit Type. - A unit containing a Phoenix Lord may take Shrouded Damage Mitigation rolls as though it did not have Fearless, as for the Primarch Unit Type. - Counts as having the Primarch Unit Type for any Wargear or Special Rule that Primarchs may ignore. - A Phoenix Lord takes up either an HQ slot or a Primarch slot, chosen by the player.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Asuryani" id="2109-d34a-117d-7e65" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>- Has the Legacies of the Fall Special Rule. - A model with the Infantry or Cavalry Unit Type and this Sub-type has the Battle Focus Special Rule.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Grav-Platform" id="5bc9-8d97-e461-8fc5" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>- If a unit with any Grav-Platform models has no models without this Sub-type, all models in the unit are immediately removed as casualties. - Cannot shoot as part of any Reaction. - May shoot Heavy or Ordnance weapons counting as Stationary, even if it moved in the previous Movement phase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Mechanised" id="694c-6f93-db24-0199" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>- Successful Wounds from Poisoned (X) or Fleshbane attacks must be re-rolled against this model. - Failed To Wound rolls with Armourbane (X) weapons against a unit including any Mechanised models must be re-rolled. - May attack with all its weapons in a Shooting Attack, including as part of a Reaction. - May fire Heavy and Ordnance weapons counting as Stationary even if it moved in the preceding Movement phase, and may Charge as normal regardless of any Shooting Attacks made that turn. - Attacks against a unit with this Sub-type are resolved as if the model had the Dreadnought Unit Type. This covers Wargear, Weapons, Special Rules, Psychic Powers, and any other abilities. - No model without the Mechanised Sub-type may join a unit containing Mechanised models.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Wraith" id="2fce-cd45-caff-8ba8" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>- Wraithsight: At the start of each of the Controlling Player's Movement phases, a unit with any Wraith models takes a Leadership test using the unmodified Leadership of a Wraith model in the unit. Units arriving or Disembarking after the start of the phase test immediately after doing so. - Pass: no penalty, and the unit may react as normal, ignoring the Automata Unit Type's limitations, until the start of its next Movement phase. - Fail: –2 to Movement, Weapon Skill, Ballistic Skill, and Initiative (also applied to any rule that uses unmodified Characteristics) until the start of its next Movement phase. - May fire all its weapons in each Shooting Attack, including as part of a Reaction where eligible. - May fire Heavy and Ordnance weapons counting as Stationary even if it moved in the preceding Movement phase, and may Charge as normal regardless of any Shooting Attacks made that turn. - Ignores Night Fighting. - Ignores Initiative penalties when Charging into or through Difficult or Dangerous Terrain. - Cannot be affected by Cybertheurgic Rites, and ignores any of their effects. - Ignores the Disruption and Haywire Special Rules. - A Detachment may include up to two Wraith units for each model with the Path of the Dead Special Rule in that Detachment.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="A Bloody-Handed God" id="bea0-dca5-f93e-b75e" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>Unlike other Daemon Primarchs, an Avatar of Khaine may never be the Warlord and may not select a Warlord Trait; choose another eligible model instead. It may never join or be joined by any other model or unit, and may not be given any Retinue during army selection.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Acrobatic" id="83ea-c189-cee6-712b" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>A unit made up entirely of models with this rule that Runs in the Movement phase may still declare a Charge in the Assault phase of the same turn. These models attack at their normal Initiative step after successfully Charging through Difficult or Dangerous Terrain, but still suffer any Charge roll penalties from that terrain.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Agile" id="ff11-6ad4-c990-5f84" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>The model may re-roll failed Shrouded Damage Mitigation rolls.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Aspect Ascendant" id="707a-b582-2e08-5a56" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>An Aspect Exarchs unit is selected as any other unit, using one Force Organisation slot. Before the first turn and before deployment, every model in it must be assigned to another unit from the same Detachment; an Exarch not assigned is immediately slain. - Each Exarch may only be assigned to a unit without the Character Sub-type (or Phoenix Lord Unit Type) that has the matching Aspect Shrine (X) rule. No more than one Exarch per unit. - Once assigned, the Exarch is part of that unit and may not leave it for any reason. - No Victory points are ever scored for removing an Exarch as a casualty. - The Exarch does not gain access to the unit's additional Wargear options.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Aspect Shrine (X)" id="ca67-1dda-6b7a-970f" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>The bracketed value names the model's Aspect Shrine. For each model in a Detachment with the Character Sub-type (or Phoenix Lord Unit Type) and a given Aspect Shrine (X), the Detachment may include up to one other non-Character unit with the matching Aspect Shrine (X). These units still need available Force Organisation slots. Dedicated Transports do not count towards these limits.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Battle Focus" id="4685-46be-c6c0-7ab4" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>A unit made up entirely of models with this rule may Run in its Movement phase and still shoot in the following Shooting phase. If it does, all its shooting attacks that phase are resolved at BS 2.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Bio-Cataclysm" id="440f-8c1c-93ac-a86a" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>If a model with a Toughness Characteristic is slain by a weapon with this rule, centre a Large Blast (5") marker over it. All models under the marker suffer an automatic hit at Strength 5, AP 5, with Ignores Cover. Models slain this way do not generate further Bio-Cataclysm markers.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Blade Spirit" id="80e3-4648-882a-bf00" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>The Controlling Player may re-roll all failed To Hit rolls of 1 for attacks made with a weapon with this rule.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Bonesinger Companions" id="1c4a-b7e3-7adc-fa49" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>A Bonesinger Conclave is selected as any other unit, using one Force Organisation slot. Before the first turn and before deployment, every Bonesinger must be assigned to another unit from the same Detachment. - Bonesingers may only be assigned to Guardian Defenders, Storm Guardians, or Vaul's Wrath Support Batteries. No more than one Bonesinger per unit. - Once assigned, the Bonesinger is part of that unit and may not leave it; if the unit is removed as a casualty, so is the Bonesinger. - No Victory points are ever scored for removing a Bonesinger as a casualty. - The Bonesinger gains the unit's special rules (except those that forbid it) and Unit Sub-types, but not access to its additional Wargear options.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Breath of Khaine" id="f716-065f-763b-7f63" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>When attacking with Wall of Death (Core Rulebook, page 248), a weapon with this rule inflicts D6 Hits instead of D3.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Brutal Ambush" id="1877-978d-232b-b517" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>The unit has Shrouded (5+) until the first time it is locked in combat. It then loses Shrouded (5+) and gains Rage (2) and Counter-Attack (1).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Communion of Minds" id="1d39-f98d-04f4-4714" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>Models with this rule in a unit containing several of them must cast Psychic Powers as a group, using the majority Leadership. When a power is manifested, choose one model as the originating model for measuring ranges. The unit's current number of models with this rule sets its Psychic Mastery, replacing any other version they had: - 1–3 models: Psychic Mastery (1). - 4–6 models: Psychic Mastery (2). - 7–10 models: Psychic Mastery (3). Models in the unit without this rule are unaffected.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Crack Shot" id="8424-9742-b274-c8df" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>The model may re-roll a single failed To Hit, To Wound, or Armour Penetration roll per turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Dawn of Twilight" id="c90b-10ff-9afe-b213" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>In any mission where the Night Fighting rules are in effect, a player whose army includes Irillyth may choose to use Night Fighting without rolling. The Controlling Player may also re-roll any dice rolled to see whether Night Fighting stays in effect during a Game Turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Disarming Strike" id="4e37-e7d7-a1df-4c7e" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>Before rolling To Hit in a challenge, Jain Zar may nominate one of the opposing model's melee weapons. Both models roll a D6 and add their Weapon Skill; the higher result wins. - If the opponent wins, Jain Zar reduces her Attacks by 3 for that Assault phase. - If Jain Zar wins, she reduces her Attacks by 1 for that Assault phase, and the opposing model counts as no longer equipped with the nominated weapon for that phase. - These modifiers ignore the Phoenix Lord Unit Type's usual restrictions.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Distortion Impalement" id="9b5e-de3e-8775-66f6" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>A weapon with this rule ignores Void Shields on its target. Before firing it, roll a D6: on a 6, the attack is resolved with the Vortex special rule.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Dragon of Myth" id="5be3-f97d-3b9a-d387" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>At the start of any Fight sub-phase, each model with this rule in base contact with an enemy makes D3 additional attacks at Initiative step 10. They are resolved at Strength 4, AP –, and count as Flame attacks.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Fast Shot" id="00e5-ee25-196d-6170" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>The model adds one to the number of shots fired when making a Shooting Attack with a Heavy weapon.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Favoured of Khaine" id="14a8-a383-8f84-8282" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>All units made up entirely of Asuryani models that can draw line of sight to at least one model with this rule gain +1 Leadership (to a maximum of 10).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Flexible Tactics" id="b814-b8c9-4bca-d877" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>At the beginning of the Controlling Player's turn, a unit containing models with this rule must choose one Tactic. Only models with Flexible Tactics benefit. - Defensive Posture: If at least half the unit's models are within 6" of an Objective, all models gain Battle-Hardened (1), Feel No Pain (5+), and Stubborn. - Offensive Rush: When the unit makes a Shooting Attack, each weapon makes one additional shot (Assault 2 becomes Assault 3, and so on).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Flickerjump" id="e4fa-3adb-e9c3-29a0" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>The unit may make the Flickerjump Advanced Reaction. Flickerjump (Advanced Reaction): May be made in the opposing player's Shooting phase when an enemy unit declares a Shooting Attack targeting a friendly unit made up entirely of models with Flickerjump. Before the attack is resolved, the target unit moves 2D6" in any direction; this distance cannot be modified. On a double 1, one model from the unit is removed as a casualty. If the attack is no longer valid after the move (no line of sight or out of range, for example), the Active player may not choose a new target and no attacks are made.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Ghostlight" id="e1a0-83e0-4456-3c24" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>When a unit with more than one model armed with Ghostlight weapons shoots, it may combine its fire. Select one model; no other model in the unit may fire a Ghostlight weapon that phase. The selected model shoots with its Ghostlight weapon (if it has several Ghostlight profiles, choose one; if only one profile has Ghostlight, use that one). For every two additional models in the unit with a Ghostlight weapon that can see the selected model, apply one of the following bonuses (the same bonus may be chosen more than once): - +6" Range. - +1 Strength (to a maximum of 10). - –1 AP (to a minimum of 1). - +1 shot.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Ghoststrike" id="a7dd-451c-59eb-c2c6" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>On any turn in which Irillyth charges a unit that has suffered at least one successful Hit from a Ghostlight weapon, the Spear of Starlight's Wanelight Glaive profile becomes Strength +3 and gains Armourbane (Melee) and Murderous Strike (5+) until the end of that player turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Guardian Artillerists" id="0b68-5288-635c-e5ef" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>A Vaul's Wrath Support Battery needs one Guardian Crew per Support Weapon for all Support Weapons to shoot. If at the start of a Shooting phase it has fewer Guardian Crew than Support Weapons, only as many Support Weapons as there are Crew may shoot. While the unit has at least as many Crew as Support Weapons, it cannot be Pinned and automatically passes Pinning tests.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Guardian Officers" id="78f4-f97f-6197-7ec8" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>A Guardian Officer Cadre is selected as any other unit, using one Force Organisation slot; a Cadre of three or more models at list creation uses no slot. Before the first turn and before deployment, every model in it must be assigned to another unit from the same Detachment. - Guardian Officers may only be assigned to Guardian Defenders, Storm Guardians, or Vaul's Wrath Support Batteries. Skyrunner Officers may only be assigned to Windriders or Windrider Support Squads. No more than one Officer per unit. - Once assigned, the Officer is part of that unit and may not leave it, but functions as normal if it is the sole survivor. - No Victory points are ever scored for removing an Officer as a casualty. - The Officer gains the unit's special rules (except those that forbid it) and Unit Sub-types, but not access to its additional Wargear options.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Guardian of the Gates" id="1a87-6582-7653-14d0" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>A model with this rule may only be selected in an army that also includes a Webway Gate. It must be assigned to Reserves and deployed using the Webway Strike rule.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Herald of Victory" id="3d89-808d-7771-7514" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>A unit containing at least one model with this rule always counts as rolling a Hit on the scatter die when making a Deep Strike Assault.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Holo-Emitter" id="7318-7e03-d38a-418b" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>The model is a Barricade and gives a 5+ Cover Save to models it obscures. Wounds from Blast attacks against a model claiming cover from it must be re-rolled.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Inescapable Accuracy" id="4645-b253-89bf-1e3e" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>Successful Shrouded Damage Mitigation rolls and Countermeasures Saves made against this model's Shooting Attacks must be re-rolled.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Iron Resolve" id="ab56-8cbb-39f7-b490" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>A unit containing one or more models with this rule automatically passes Pinning tests, Regroup tests, and Morale checks, and ignores the Fear special rule.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Khaine Awakened" id="f736-5a8b-cfaa-b77c" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>All friendly Asuryani units within 12" of the Avatar of Khaine that can draw line of sight to it gain Rage (2) and Stubborn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Legacies of the Fall" id="de6c-1d83-6121-1248" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>The model has Hatred (Daemons). The unit also suffers –1 Leadership while locked in a combat that includes at least one Daemon model; this stacks with other Leadership penalties.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Linked Fire" id="9073-ff0b-02a6-6fcf" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>When a unit of more than one model, made up entirely of models armed with Linked Fire weapons, shoots, it may make a Linked Fire attack. Select one model; no other model in the unit may fire a Linked Fire weapon that phase. If the weapon has several Linked Fire profiles, choose one; if only one profile has Linked Fire, use that one. For each additional model in the unit with a Linked Fire weapon that can see the selected model, apply one of the following bonuses (the same bonus may be chosen more than once): - +2 Strength. - +1 to rolls on the Vehicle Damage table. - +1 shot. - Brutal (2), or +2 to an existing Brutal (X) value.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Mark of Kurnous" id="33ba-4dc2-f5e0-a8e8" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>At the start of the controlling player's Shooting phase, the unit may select an enemy unit within 12" of any of its models. Until the end of that phase, the unit loses any Firing Protocols (X) it has and instead gains Ignores Cover for Shooting Attacks against the selected unit.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Monofilament" id="f095-2ee4-6c9f-f939" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>When rolling To Wound normally against a non-Vehicle model, use the target's Initiative instead of its Toughness; Toughness still decides Instant Death. Any unit hit by one or more Monofilament attacks takes an Initiative test once the attack is resolved. If failed, it reduces its Initiative and Movement by 2 until the end of its Controlling Player's next turn. These penalties are cumulative and apply to later Initiative tests, but models with a starting Wounds of 6 or more cannot have their Characteristics reduced this way.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Mysterious Statuary" id="0e3c-8585-8923-3901" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>After Deployment Zones are determined, but before other models deploy, the Webway Gate must be set up: - Place the 2 Wraithbone Arches to form an arch with their bases 5" apart. - It must be at least 6" from the opposing player's Deployment Zone. - It may not be placed in Difficult, Dangerous, or Impassable Terrain, or inside a Building or Fortification. Asuryani units gain Stubborn while within 3" of a Webway Gate. Any model in cover behind a Wraithbone Arch has a 5+ Cover Save.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Paired Weapons" id="2374-c26b-7ec5-87ff" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>A model armed with a weapon with this rule gains an extra Attack.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Path of Command" id="2062-877a-504a-574b" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>If the army has any models with Path of Command in its Primary Detachment, one of them must be the Warlord. Models in the same Detachment as that Warlord, and with the same Aspect Shrine (X) as the Warlord (if it has one), gain the Line Sub-type.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Path of the Dead" id="f08c-999a-7268-9a39" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>The model gains the Runes of Twilight Psychic Discipline, plus Thaumaturgy from the Core Rulebook (page 322). - The army may select up to two Wraith units in the same Detachment per model with this rule. A model with both this rule and the Wraith Sub-type counts against its own allowance. - A model with this rule and Independent Character may join a unit of Automata with the Wraith Sub-type (the unit must have both).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Path of the Farseer" id="f1c7-1d03-8a66-b3bd" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>The model gains the Runes of Fate Psychic Discipline, plus Divination, Telepathy, and Thaumaturgy from the Core Rulebook (page 322).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Path of the Shaper" id="e58e-30b7-5d57-7ae1" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>All Infantry models in a unit including at least one model with this rule gain Feel No Pain (5+). This does not stack for multiple models with the rule, and Grav-Platform models do not benefit. At the start of the Controlling Player's Shooting phase, the model may give up conferring Feel No Pain (5+) and gain Battlesmith (3+) instead. It may use Battlesmith as normal, or use it on a Grav-Platform model to restore a single lost Wound, affecting any applicable friendly model within 6". This lasts until the start of the Controlling Player's next turn, when the model loses Battlesmith (3+) and regains Feel No Pain (5+).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Precise Throw" id="f95d-13a1-b7aa-1d4e" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>Immediately after a unit completes a Deep Strike Assault, one model in it may make a Shooting Attack with a weapon with this rule; only one model per unit may do so. This counts as a Shooting Attack in the Movement phase. The unit may still shoot in the following Shooting phase, but must target the same unit, and cannot shoot if no viable targets remain in it. The weapon cannot be used in any other situation.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Psychic Mastery (X)" id="55fb-981b-c675-567c" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>The model may cast up to X Psychic Powers per phase, despite the normal limits. A Psychic Power counted as a Shooting Attack counts as one power or weapon for this rule, and each power or weapon may only be cast once per phase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Riposte (X)" id="116c-fd6c-c259-62b5" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>Models attacking a model wielding a weapon with this rule subtract X from their Weapon Skill.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Runes of Warding" id="9fd9-3a2b-6877-97d5" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>Any enemy model within 18" and line of sight of a model with this rule reduces its Leadership by 3 when making Psychic checks. This is not cumulative; no model suffers penalties from more than one model with this rule.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Runes of Witnessing" id="f5a2-8261-e740-72de" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>Once per Game Turn, the model may re-roll any number of dice when making a Psychic check.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Scorpion's Sting (X)" id="0da5-3dc2-9526-5b39" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>The model causes X immediate Hits with this weapon at Initiative step 10, but may not assign any further attacks to it. This does not grant an additional Pile In move.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Seer Council Retinue" id="f2bd-4bc6-76d7-4127" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>In a Detachment with at least one Path of the Farseer model, a Seer Council may be selected as a Retinue Squad instead of an Elites choice. Choose one Path of the Farseer model from the same Detachment as its Leader. - The Retinue Squad uses no Force Organisation slot, counts as part of the Leader's unit, and does not count towards 0-1 limits. - It must deploy with the Leader, who may not voluntarily leave it. - All its models gain Chosen Warriors. - If the Leader has a Skyrunner Jetbike, the whole squad must have Skyrunner Jetbikes; if not, none may.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Shadow of Death" id="05bb-b020-1918-b1a9" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>An enemy unit with at least one model within 12" of a model with this rule rolls an additional D6 for any Leadership check, discarding the lowest. Fearless models are not affected.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Shield of Grace" id="cd3e-5b35-1f19-dc75" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>Whenever Asurmen fights in a Challenge, his Invulnerable Save improves to 3+.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Skyhunter" id="9278-e4d6-2262-be0b" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>When the model moves Flat Out, it moves up to triple its Movement instead of double.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Skyleap" id="6f1b-e76b-0b4e-608e" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>At the beginning of the Controlling Player's Movement phase, a unit made up entirely of models with this rule that is not locked in combat may be placed back into ongoing Reserves. It may then be assigned to a Deep Strike Assault as normal on the next player turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Skystrike" id="5b47-e566-83b9-6c1a" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>At the end of the Movement phase, the unit may make one Attack per model against an enemy Flyer it moved over that turn. It hits automatically on a 4+ and is resolved at Strength 4, AP 4, with Haywire. Vehicles are hit on their Side Armour. Only one target per turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Sonic Pulse" id="b95c-6859-9c9b-8f23" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>Place the Blast (3") marker touching the weapon's barrel. Instead of scattering it, move it in a straight line away from the firer, in any direction within the weapon's 45° forward arc, until it reaches maximum range or leaves the battlefield. Every model it passes over suffers one automatic Hit. Flyers cannot be hit. Knights, Titans, Super-Heavy Vehicles, Buildings, and Fortifications are hit at Strength 8.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Soul-Shatter" id="27e7-54d9-71c5-d8f2" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>Successful Invulnerable Saves against Wounds from a weapon with this rule must be re-rolled.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Soul Tear" id="e038-90d4-cabf-24e7" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>A unit including a Psyker and a weapon or ability with this rule may activate it before attacking with that weapon or resolving that ability, by making a single Psychic check with any Psyker in the unit. - Pass: for that phase, attacks with Soul Tear gain Armourbane (Melee), Armourbane (Ranged), and Fleshbane, and count as having Force for any rule affected by it. - Fail: no benefit, but the unit attacks as normal.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Stalker" id="18a1-b875-a6f3-b4f5" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>In the first round of a Challenge, the model gains bonus attacks equal to the amount by which its Initiative exceeds its opponent's. No effect if its Initiative is equal or lower.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Sun's Brilliance" id="28c7-978f-2761-3899" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>Shooting Attacks made as part of an Interceptor Reaction against a unit containing a model with this rule are resolved as Snap Shots. Models immune to Blind are not affected.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="The Runes of War" id="b1f8-839a-d825-5e86" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>The model does not pick Psychic Powers individually. It knows the Thaumaturgy Discipline and all powers from the Runes of Battle Discipline. When it is part of any unit that is not a Seer Council, it instead picks a single power from the Runes of Battle.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Unquenchable Resolve" id="b015-0bd4-b79b-69b9" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>At the end of any phase in which the model suffers one or more unsaved Wounds, its Strength and Attacks increase by 1 for each unsaved Wound. These bonuses last for the rest of the game. Damage Mitigation rolls do not prevent this.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Vector Dancer" id="8383-7604-8572-483a" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>The Flyer may make an additional 90° pivot at the end of its move in the Controlling Player's Movement phase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Vortex" id="26e7-ca1a-02ce-f1d8" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>Once an attack with this rule is resolved, its Blast markers stay in play for the rest of the battle as Vortex markers. The area under one is Area Terrain with these effects: - No line of sight may be drawn through, into, or out of it. - Any model that enters it, or begins its Controlling Player's Movement phase in it, suffers one Str 10, AP 1 Hit with Instant Death and Armourbane (Melee). A Vehicle suffering a Penetrating Hit this way adds +3 to its Vehicle Damage roll. - It gives no Cover Save, and models inside may not use Cover Saves from any other source.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="War Shout" id="885e-624f-59b7-ed3a" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>On a turn in which a unit containing a model with this rule charges or is successfully charged, enemy models locked in that combat suffer –1 Weapon Skill (to a minimum of 1).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Warlord: Cry of the Wind" id="3b89-561a-5218-0d57" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>Baharroth automatically has this Trait if he is the Warlord and may not select any other. Swooping Hawk Aspect Shrine models in his army gain Hit &amp; Run and Reaping Blow (1). An army with Baharroth gains an additional Reaction in the opposing player's Movement phase while he has not been removed as a casualty.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Warlord: Fate Reader" id="1f4b-6eab-de14-09a7" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>Eldrad Ulthran automatically has this Trait if he is the Warlord and may not select any other. At the start of the battle, before deployment, up to three Infantry or Cavalry units in the army may be given Infiltrate and Scout. The army may make an additional Reaction in any one phase of the Controlling Player's choice once per turn while the Warlord has not been removed as a casualty.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Warlord: Hand of Asuryan" id="72c4-8529-2e9e-a4e3" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>Asurmen automatically has this Trait if he is the Warlord and may not select any other. All other Aspect Shrine (X) models in his army gain Stubborn; Dire Avenger Aspect Shrine models may also use his Leadership instead of their own. The army may make an additional Reaction in any one phase per turn (not declared in advance) while the Warlord has not been removed as a casualty.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Warlord: Rhana Dandra" id="d10b-49a0-217e-77e9" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>Fuegan automatically has this Trait if he is the Warlord and may not select any other. Fire Dragon Aspect Shrine models in his army gain Dragon of Myth and Feel No Pain (5+). The army may make an additional Reaction in the Shooting phase while the Warlord has not been removed as a casualty.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Warlord: Reaper of Souls" id="40e0-3cc2-453c-de83" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>Irillyth automatically has this Trait if he is the Warlord and may not select any other. Shadow Spectre Aspect Shrine models in his army gain Ignores Cover and Night Vision. An army with Irillyth gains an additional Reaction in the opposing player's Shooting phase while he has not been removed as a casualty.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Warlord: Storm of Silence" id="e019-fd1c-d900-3891" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>Jain Zar automatically has this Trait if she is the Warlord and may not select any other. Howling Banshee Aspect Shrine models in her army gain Crusader and Furious Charge (1). The army may make an additional Reaction in the Assault phase while the Warlord has not been removed as a casualty.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Warlord: The Duellist's Fury" id="3cb6-0280-c11d-502f" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>Karandras automatically has this Trait if he is the Warlord and may not select any other. On a turn in which a Striking Scorpion Aspect Shrine unit charges or is successfully charged, it gains Riposte (1) and +1 to its Counter-Attack (X) and Rage (X) values. The army may make an additional Reaction in the Assault phase while the Warlord has not been removed as a casualty.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Warlord: The Lancer's Charge" id="ecb3-6302-a532-cb39" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>Drastanta automatically has this Trait if they are the Warlord and may not select any other. Once per game, in the Controlling Player's Charge phase, declare a Lance Charge: until the end of that Charge phase, Shining Spear Aspect Shrine models in the army roll an additional die for Charge distance and discard the lowest, and count their Hammer of Wrath (X) as one higher. The army may make an additional Reaction in the Movement phase while the Warlord has not been removed as a casualty.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Warlord: The Reaper's Gaze" id="7337-1e2d-b951-9176" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>Maugan Ra automatically has this Trait if he is the Warlord and may not select any other. After deployment, but before the first turn, nominate a single enemy unit. Dark Reaper Aspect Shrine models gain Precision Shots (5+) and Precision Strikes (5+) when attacking it. The army may make an additional Reaction in the Shooting phase while the Warlord has not been removed as a casualty.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Webway Strike" id="5ee7-a4f0-358a-803c" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>Before Game Turn 1, when placing units in Reserve, a player with a Webway Gate may assign one or more Reserve units to a Webway Strike. - From Turn 2, the Controlling Player may deploy one assigned unit per turn without a Reserve roll, moving on as though the line between the Wraithbone Arches were their battlefield edge. - Enemy units with models within 6" of the arriving unit take an immediate Pinning test. Then any enemy units not Pinned or Falling Back, and in line of sight and range, may make the Interceptor Advanced Reaction against it. No other Reaction may be made against this deployment. - The arriving unit may not Move or Run that Movement phase, but may Shoot and Assault as normal. - If no Wraithbone Arch remains in play, units assigned to a Webway Strike return to Reserves.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Whirlwind of Death" id="a17e-1487-c7aa-7bc7" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>Maugan Ra may fire The Maugetar twice in the Controlling Player's Shooting phase, and these attacks may target different units.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Wraith Conclave" id="62c1-b455-a665-6b9e" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>When deployed (at the start of the battle or from Reserves), all models in the unit are placed in coherency, but afterwards each operates independently as its own unit, including for Victory Points and Units Destroyed.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Wraithbone Core" id="8a00-d656-8608-bc40" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>The model ignores all Psychic Powers and Cybertheurgic Rites, and attacks by Psychic and Cybertheurgic Weapons. It also ignores Haywire and Disruption (X); such weapons must damage it normally using their Strength. When destroyed, its Catastrophic Damage is resolved at AP 2.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Invulnerable Save (X)" id="a59c-ba92-c096-58d8" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>The model has an Invulnerable Save of X, which may be taken against any Wound instead of its armour save.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Multi-Part Fortification" id="5fa9-e87f-754d-77b3" hidden="false" publicationId="d5ae-9e15-7ef2-10f7">
      <description>Listed on this datasheet but not defined in the conversion doc.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
